WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.176 --> 00:00:02.140
- Some people may think,

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:05.245
how can it be that somebody
can both gay and a cowboy,

00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:10.086
because the cowboy is the model
of the macho, masculine man.

00:00:10.086 --> 00:00:12.582
But it doesn't matter whether
you're a man or a woman,

00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:15.164
whether you're a butch or nelly,

00:00:15.164 --> 00:00:18.217
everybody can find a
place within our community

00:00:18.217 --> 00:00:19.706
and within our rodeo circuit.

00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:21.206
That's who we are.

00:00:22.546 --> 00:00:25.296
(crowd cheering)

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:28.278
My name is Bruce Gros,

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:31.941
and I'm the president of the
International Gay Rodeo Association.

00:00:31.941 --> 00:00:33.612
We're celebrating our 30th anniversary

00:00:33.612 --> 00:00:35.689
of our finals rodeo today.

00:00:35.689 --> 00:00:38.138
Cowboys and cowgirls compete in 13 events,

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.916
so that the best of the
best are represented

00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:43.171
in our sport at this event today.

00:00:43.171 --> 00:00:44.314
- My name is Greg Begay,

00:00:44.314 --> 00:00:46.742
and I'm an All Around Cowboy, and I'm gay.

00:00:46.742 --> 00:00:48.791
I grew up on the Navajo reservation.

00:00:48.791 --> 00:00:51.747
Being on the reservation,
you kinda find things to do,

00:00:51.747 --> 00:00:54.363
and rodeo was one of them.

00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:56.961
Gay rodeo is more than just a celebration.

00:00:56.961 --> 00:00:59.322
I think it's a place for
people to be comfortable.

00:00:59.322 --> 00:01:02.989
I don't have to worry
about hiding anything.

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:08.679
(announcer speaking)
(crowd cheering)

00:01:08.679 --> 00:01:11.218
- Years ago, professional
cowboys looked upon us

00:01:11.218 --> 00:01:12.936
as mocking their sport.

00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:14.084
As they've come to know us more,

00:01:14.084 --> 00:01:15.843
they've come to appreciate
and understand the fact

00:01:15.843 --> 00:01:18.868
that we embrace the same sport they do.

00:01:18.868 --> 00:01:20.713
We may express it a
little bit differently,

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:21.808
but we still have the same passion

00:01:21.808 --> 00:01:24.063
and dedication to being good competitors,

00:01:24.063 --> 00:01:27.342
good cowboys and good
cowgirls that they do.

00:01:27.342 --> 00:01:29.886
- Gay rodeo offers a few different events

00:01:29.886 --> 00:01:31.678
that traditional rodeo doesn't.

00:01:31.678 --> 00:01:35.261
We offer wild drag
race, and goat dressing.

00:01:37.494 --> 00:01:40.359
- [Bruce] In our rodeo,
men and women can compete

00:01:40.359 --> 00:01:42.321
in every event equally.

00:01:42.321 --> 00:01:44.826
You're gonna see men in drag.

00:01:44.826 --> 00:01:46.927
I don't know that when people
really come to know us,

00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:49.698
they're gonna find a
more warm, supportive,

00:01:49.698 --> 00:01:52.847
friendly experience than
they'll find here with us.

00:01:52.847 --> 00:01:55.103
- [Greg] Gay rodeo is
a safe space for people

00:01:55.103 --> 00:01:57.068
to be accepted with each other.

00:01:57.068 --> 00:01:59.404
I've established a rodeo family here.

00:01:59.404 --> 00:02:01.245
I can always count on people,

00:02:01.245 --> 00:02:02.278
and they can count on me.

00:02:02.278 --> 00:02:05.111
(inspiring music)

